# Ecommerce architecture

bermooda is a single-shop, open-source ecommerce platform. One React Router app serves the storefront, admin back office, and REST API.

## Surfaces

| Surface | Route prefix | UI location |
| ------- | ------------ | ----------- |
| Storefront | `/` (via `app/routes/storefront/`) | Active theme in `app/themes/<name>/components/` |
| Admin | `/admin/*` | Core-owned UI in `app/components/admin/` |
| Public API | `/api/v1/*` | Thin route handlers over `app/core/*` |
| Admin API | `/api/admin/v1/*` | API-key auth; thin handlers over `app/core/*` |
| Webhooks | `/webhooks/:provider` | Generic dispatcher to payment/shipping providers |
| Auth handlers | `/admin/auth/*`, `/account/auth/*` | Proxies to better-auth (`app/routes/auth/`) |

Plugin dispatchers (static routes, not runtime mutation): `/admin/plugins/:pluginId/*`, `/apps/:pluginId/*`.

All public URLs must be registered in [app/routes.js](mdc:app/routes.js).

## Layering

- **Routes** orchestrate loaders/actions and call `app/core/*`.
- **`app/core/*`** owns domain logic (catalog, cart, checkout, orders, payments, etc.).
- **Themes** render storefront UI only. Theme components receive data from route loaders; they do not import `app/core/*` server modules directly. Client-safe helpers come from `#/core/index.js`.
- **Plugins** extend via manifests, hooks, blocks, and optional admin/storefront route descriptors resolved by static dispatchers. See [docs/plugins.md](mdc:docs/plugins.md).

Do not put ecommerce domain workflows in `app/services`, `app/utils`, or `app/components`.

## Themes

- Each theme lives under `app/themes/<name>/` with `manifest.js`, `components/`, and optional `i18n/<locale>.json`.
- Storefront page components belong in the active theme, not in `app/components/`.
- Theme engine: `#/core/themes/index.server`. See [docs/themes.md](mdc:docs/themes.md).

## Plugins

- Each plugin lives under `app/plugins/<id>/` with `manifest.js`, optional `index.server.js` (hooks), `admin/routes.js`, and `blocks/`.
- Plugin engine: `#/core/plugins/index.server`. See [docs/plugins.md](mdc:docs/plugins.md).

## Dual auth

Admin/staff and customers are **separate** better-auth instances with isolated cookies and models. See [docs/auth.md](mdc:docs/auth.md).

| Audience | Server module | Client module | Base path |
| -------- | ------------- | ------------- | --------- |
| Admin/staff | `#/libs/auth/admin/index.server` | `#/libs/auth/admin-client` | `/admin/auth` |
| Customer | `#/libs/auth/customer/index.server` | `#/libs/auth/customer-client` | `/account/auth` |

Protect routes with `adminAuthMiddleware` / `customerAuthMiddleware`, or call `authenticate(request)` / `getCustomerSession(request)` in layout loaders — follow the pattern in the nearest sibling route.

## i18n and locale

Storefront locale is **cookie-driven**, not encoded in URL paths. Resolution lives in `app/core/i18n/`.

## Emails

- Shop transactional emails: `app/emails/shop/` (order confirmation, shipping, etc.).
- Auth emails: `app/emails/templates/`.
- Queue via `#/emails/job.server`.
